":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/6551","id":543583208,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU0MzU4MzIwOA==","user":{"login":"ojw28","id":7881572,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4ODE1NzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7881572?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28","html_url":"https://github.com/ojw28","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2019-10-18T08:01:22Z","updated_at":"2019-10-18T08:01:22Z","body":"It's unfortunate that the HLS specification has defined it that way...\r\n\r\n> The player should use frame resolution instead of display resolution when querying video capabilities as frame resolution is what decoder cares. For mp4 files, frame resolution can be extracted from width and height in Sample Description box. For TS files, the player has to inspect SPS to extract the frame resolution.\r\n\r\nIt's infeasible to implement this efficiently, since it would require downloading the start of every variant prior to the start of playback. The increased latency doesn't seem like an acceptable tradeoff, so I think it's better to leave things as they are now. Note that the commit referenced above should solve the problem in practice unless the display and frame resolutions are significantly different, which is not something we've seen in practice.","author_association":"CONTRIBU